{"id": "actor/act-ops", "type": "actor", "slug": "act-ops", "path": "knowledge/actors/act-ops.md", "frontmatter": {"type": "actor", "created": "2026-01-15", "updated": "2026-01-15", "draft": false, "title": "Ops", "description": "The default build target runs `dotnet test Example.Tests.csproj --filter \"TestCategory = Smoke Tests\"`, and any failure fails the build. The other UI fixtures and the whole API project are built but never run by the checked-in build."}, "body": "<!-- one line \u2014 who this role is, in the product's own words. Use cases point here through `actor`; \"what can this role do\" is that edge inverted. -->\n\n## Goals\n\n<!-- what this role is trying to get done, not what the product offers -->\n\n## Permissions\n\n<!-- what this role may and may not do, as the rules the product enforces -->"}
